## Operator semantics reminder (DO NOT VIOLATE)
    • create   – new symbol/sort/assertion that didn’t exist before.
    • replace  – *complete* re-declaration of an existing target.  Use this
                to extend an enum (add variants) while keeping its name.
    • remove   – delete the target altogether.

## Constraints
    1. Return either a single object **or** a list of objects, BUT NO
        extra text or markdown fencing.
    2. For `"target.kind":"assertion"` you **must** give an
        `"assert_tag": "R<req>_<k>"` that identifies which requirement
        the assertion belongs to.